# Creating Templates

This guide walks you through creating and editing email templates using the built-in editor.

## Accessing the Template Editor

To create a new template:

1. Navigate to your event
2. Click the **Emails** tab
3. Click **Create Template**

To edit an existing template, click on it in the template list.

## Template Details

### Name

Give your template a descriptive name that helps you identify it later (e.g., "VIP Invitation - English", "Final Reminder").

### Type

Select the template type that matches its purpose:

- Invitation, Reminder, Confirmation
- Declined Acknowledgment, Update, Cancellation
- Custom

### Category (Optional)

Optionally associate the template with a guest category. This helps organize templates and can be used for category-specific communications.

### Default Template

Check this option to make this template the default for its type. Only one template can be the default for each type within an event.

## Writing Content

The template editor has three content fields:

### Subject Line

The email subject that recipients see in their inbox. Keep it clear and compelling. You can include variables like `{{event.name}}` for personalization.

### HTML Content

The main email body using HTML formatting. The editor provides:

- **Syntax Highlighting** - HTML tags are color-coded for readability
- **Line Numbers** - Easy reference for longer templates
- **Code Folding** - Collapse sections to focus on specific areas

{% callout type="info" %}
Basic HTML knowledge is helpful but not required. You can write plain text and add simple formatting tags like `<b>bold</b>` and `<i>italic</i>`.
{% /callout %}

### Plain Text (Optional)

A text-only version of the email for recipients who can't view HTML emails. If left empty, a plain text version will be auto-generated from the HTML content.

## Language Tabs

Switch between English and Arabic content using the tabs above the editor:

### English (EN)

The primary content tab. English content is required.

### Arabic (AR)

Optional Arabic translation. When editing Arabic content:

- The editor automatically switches to right-to-left mode
- Text alignment and direction are adjusted
- The preview will display with RTL formatting

{% callout type="info" %}
You can create English-only templates initially and add Arabic translations later.
{% /callout %}

## Saving Templates

Click **Save Template** to save your changes. The system validates:

- Template name is provided
- English subject line is provided
- English HTML content is provided

## Editing Existing Templates

To modify a template:

1. Click the template in the list
2. Make your changes in the editor
3. Click **Save Template**

Changes take effect immediately for future use of the template.

## Duplicating Templates

To create a copy of an existing template:

1. Click the actions menu (three dots) on a template
2. Select **Duplicate**
3. A new template is created with "(Copy)" appended to the name
4. Edit the duplicate as needed

This is useful when creating variations for different categories or slightly different messaging.
